  "mechanism": {
    "outer_edge_rejection": "Without a source-backed outer ASCII space on either side, optional normalization cannot produce mandatory removable padding. Reject before copying or projecting the body.",
    "source_partition_reuse": "Padding fragments need source IDs only. They use the same selected-versus-outside source intersection check as ordinary slices, preserving rejection of a multi-scalar glyph shared by padding and body.",
    "redundant_body_removed": "The original interval is already source-validated. Every moved cut is validated from its padding side against all other backed tokens; the caller projects the retained body before emitting its refinement. The discarded intermediate body copy adds no separate validity condition.",
    "budget_accounting": "Normalization/token scans and padding source-partition visits are charged separately. Actual removed materializations are no longer charged. Preset limits, candidate conventions, optional certificates and original-cut mappings remain unchanged."
  },
